\end{equation}
In this case, we will say that $a'$ is \emph{uniformly distributed} on  $S$.

We also note that if $S \subseteq [N/V]$ and $a'':[N/V] \to \mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z}$ is any function that agrees with $a$ on $[N/V] \setminus S$, then
\begin{align}\label{E: equivalence of lambdas'}
