\end{align*}
where in the second-to-last line we split the sum at $t = 1/\|V\theta\|_{\mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z}}$.  This quantity is $\ll N/(V w^c)$ unless $\norm{V\theta}_{\mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z}}<V w^{cd}/N$.

We now analyze when the contribution of $\tilde{\nu}$ can be large.  By \cite[Proposition 4.3]{GT12} and \cite[Lemma A.10]{Leng23b}, we have
$$\abs{N^{(d-1)/d}W_d^{1/d} \sum_{z \in [(N/W_d)^{1/d}V^{-1}]}e(\theta \widetilde P(Vz+r'))} \ll \frac{N}{Vw^c}$$
